experiment: blockanchor
  instrument        blockanchor   trial seed 0000000001352c69   2000 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  question          `blockwhere` showed ONE neuron costs 30% of the lesson at
                    the top of the group and 7% in the middle. Does that
                    survive at a USEFUL size -- half the group?
  the comparison    the two complementary halves, which is exactly what a
                    separated pair of lessons would occupy. top7 leaves the
                    lesson the LOWER half; bot7 leaves it the UPPER half.
  read it carefully a cheap bot7 with an expensive top7 does NOT make
                    separation affordable. Separation needs BOTH halves at
                    once, so that result would say the leverage is
                    CONCENTRATED AT ONE END and only one lesson can have it
                    -- which points at making the readout uniform, not at
                    finding a cheaper place to put a mask.
  the anchor        top7 must reproduce ~53%, which `compartprobe` measured
                    for these seven neurons on this genome and code.

